{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
The wind came howling off the [Eb]hills
[Bb]The waves broke over the [F]side
[Bb]The boat was filling fast [Eb]with water
[Bb]And the [F]fishermen [Bb]cried
But Jesus slept down in the [Eb]stern
[Bb]His head upon [F]a pillow
[Bb]Teacher, don't you [Eb]care at all
[Bb]We're go[F]ing down be[Bb]low
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Quiet, be still, he said [Eb]to the sea
And [Bb]the wind lay down at his [F]feet
Who is [Bb]this man, who [Eb]can this be
Even [Bb]the wind and [F]the waves o[Bb]bey
{end_of_chorus}

