{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
He rose and spoke into the [Eb]gale
[Bb]And all the storm was [F]gone
[Bb]The water lay as [Eb]smooth as glass
Be[Bb]neath the morn[F]ing [Bb]sun
Why are you so [Eb]afraid, he said
[Bb]Do you still [F]have no faith
[Bb]They trembled in the [Eb]quiet boat
[Bb]And looked [F]into his [Bb]face
{end_of_verse}

